2.)  the printer number as it appears in the lf and sd parameters


Here is the entry in the printer error logfile which I am referring to:

#tail -6 /var/adm/lp10err
<<
pcfof Warning:
        XF mode and auto passthru are not permitted when accounting
        is specified. Switching to ASCII filter mode.
>>
Filter 'f' terminated (sig=-1,err=0)
#


Here is a copy of the printcap entry:

#
lp10|10|lp10|willow11_printer:\
        :if=/usr/lbin/pcfof +Chplj4000tn.pcf:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lp10err:\
        :lp=@willow11/hp16:\
        :mx#0:\
        :of=/usr/lbin/pcfof +Chplj4000tn.pcf:\
        :pl#66:\
        :pw#180:\
        :rw:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd10:\
        :xf=/usr/lbin/xf:
# 
  
Notice that the af parameter is not set for these printers ...

Does anyone have an idea as to why these error messages are being generated?   
Also, how can these errors be avoided?

I would appreciate any insights into this problem and its recommended 
resolution.    

Thanks !!!

                         


