Solution from Dr. Thomas P. Blinn:

Won't work.  In V4.0x it was relatively easy to "clone" a system disk
even onto a quite different system type.  On V5.x, there is a way to
use one system to load the software, but once it's configured it's
pretty strongly tied to the specific system on which it was booted.
And the methods for installing the software and then moving the disk
to a different system are NOT well documented (if they're documented
at all).

Do a clean install on the DS20E.  It's easier.

