We were running Tru64 5.1 Patch Kit 5. I had a look through the release =
notes for Patch Kit 6 (which was released in April), and found the =
following entry:
Patch 1163:
Fixes a kernel memory fault in tcp_rad_slowtimo. This patch also
fixes a kernel memory fault in soclose() before calling soabort for
listener sockets.

So it looks like the tcp_rad_slowtimo function caused the problems. This =
was confirmed by HP Support.

